From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Faye-Lund <erik.faye-lund@arm.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:09:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: drop redundant descriptor-copy

We're already doing this in prepare_draw(), by calling
panvk_draw_prepare_fs_copy_desc_job(). Doing this again is redundant,
even if we never queue the redundant work.

But it's actually a bit worse than that, because we also fail to
initialize ptr in the case where cmdbuf->state.gfx.fs.required is false,
meaning that we risk undefined behavior here.

So let's just remove the whole block here. It shouldn't be needed, and
it can cause harm.

CID: 1696341
Fixes: e705ac9c00df ("panvk/jm: Take a desc_info in meta_get_copy_desc_job")
Fixes: 743b41a28446 ("panvk: Use IDVS jobs when we can")
Reviewed-by: Boris Brezillon <boris.brezillon@collabora.com>
(cherry picked from commit 42f5036eb2f9a26c1785de562ded1193ae288431)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45704>
(cherry picked from commit 85d20a4648d)

Backported to the 26.2.4-based fork: the src/ hunks applied as is; .pick_status.json (not in the fork's
history as such) was left out.

Generated-by: LLM
